# Copy to app/.env and fill in. Never commit app/.env — it is gitignored.
#
# Expo loads .env from the project root, which for this repo is app/, not the
# repository root. The .env.example at the repository root lists the same key
# for the pipeline's benefit; this is the one the mobile app actually reads.
#
# EXPO_PUBLIC_ is not a decoration: Expo only inlines variables with that prefix
# into the client bundle, and this key is a public SDK key meant to ship in a
# client. Secret keys must never carry the prefix and must never be used here.
#
# Where to get the value:
#
#   RevenueCat dashboard -> Apps & providers -> your app -> public SDK key.
#
# A key beginning `test_` is a RevenueCat Test Store key: purchases run entirely
# on RevenueCat's side, entitlements and renewals behave for real, and no store
# account, product review or money is involved. That is the right key for
# development and for recording a demo. The SDK deliberately refuses to run a
# release build configured with one, so it can never reach production by
# accident.
#
# Changing this file's values requires restarting the bundler with the cache
# cleared (`npx expo start -c`) — EXPO_PUBLIC_ variables are inlined at build
# time, so a warm bundler keeps serving the previous value.
EXPO_PUBLIC_REVENUECAT_PUBLIC_SDK_KEY=
